045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281283 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281283 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186280720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281283 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ff6d4ed4-6f38-58ef-90e7-56012b55823a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281332 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281332 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161802" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281332 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281332 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the Jacobian determinant of the transformation $T:(u,v,w)\\to (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)),$ given that \n\n$$\nu=3x+yz,\\,v=z,\\,w=-y.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281332 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "78cdb0a8-90d4-5ce3-9ce4-dfaf056d437e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281332 #edb/ref 1074 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, we're only given ${T}^{-1}.$ So, we compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute $\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)},$ the Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\n- Then, we will compute the Jacobian determinant of $T$ using the relation\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & =3 & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y} & =z & \\,\\frac{∂u}{∂z} & =y \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂y} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂v}{∂z} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂y} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂w}{∂z} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant of ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} & \\frac{∂u}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y} & \\frac{∂v}{∂z} \\\\ \\frac{∂w}{∂x} & \\frac{∂w}{∂y} & \\frac{∂w}{∂z}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & z & y \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(0+1) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & ={(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186281342 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186280850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281342 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161818" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281342 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281342 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+3w \\\\ v+2w \\\\ {v}^{2}-u\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186281342 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5828c68b-3870-5e91-8f73-8351ac68b7ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281342 #edb/ref 1074 "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u+3w,\\,y(u,v,w)=v+2w,\\,z(u,v,w)={v}^{2}-u.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =3 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =2v & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(0-4v)+3(0+1) \\\\  & =3-4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 3-4v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $3-4v=0$ defines the plane $v=\\frac{3}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186324062 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324062 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324062 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a3dfa61-4983-5101-a590-b7cae3069606" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324490 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{w}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324490 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324490 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "408e29c9-6522-5467-9ab8-def9fe8cfb65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324714 #edb/ref 1080 "16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324714 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324714 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5975b6e2-4d63-5522-bc15-85311b4304c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324848 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{w}{u}^{2}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324848 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324848 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "69224e59-e1c5-54cd-8748-b2d597b5cd76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325004 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{w}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325004 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325004 #edb/ref 1083