partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ w & 0 & u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & u\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ w & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(u-0)+2(0-w) \\\\  & =u-2w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ u-2w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $u-2w=0$ defines the plane $u=2w.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186401276 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401276 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401276 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401276 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401280 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401276 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401276 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401276 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401276 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186401281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401276 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "65676948-b2fa-585d-8619-ca89f50c6f34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401277 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the plane $u+v-2w=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401277 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401277 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "53f14d31-90ea-5326-97dc-45022d0835ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401278 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the elliptic cylinder ${u}^{2}+2{w}^{2}=1.$" #edb/ref 17592